BOINC docker_wrapper: use only the GPU assigned by the client.

The wrapper passes all GPUs into the container ("--gpus all" or the CDI device
"nvidia.com/gpu=all") and does not pass on which GPU the client assigned to the task
(gpu_device_num in init_data.xml; the client does not add "--device N" to the command
line of these apps either). On a host with several NVIDIA GPUs all tasks therefore ran
on the first one (CUDA's default device) while the client counted the others as busy.
The wrapper now sets CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=<gpu_device_num> in the container for NVIDIA
GPUs. It uses CUDA's device order, the same order the client numbers its NVIDIA devices
in, not the PCI order of nvidia-smi and the CDI device names, so it also holds for
hosts with different GPU models. nvidia-smi inside the container still lists all GPUs.
A container that already exists (task restarted) keeps the device it was created with.
Written for server_release/1.6/1.6.2 on top of 0002 and 0004 to 0006.

diff --git a/samples/docker_wrapper/docker_wrapper.cpp b/samples/docker_wrapper/docker_wrapper.cpp
index 62876cf..16c49fd 100644
--- a/samples/docker_wrapper/docker_wrapper.cpp
+++ b/samples/docker_wrapper/docker_wrapper.cpp
@@ -711,6 +711,20 @@ int create_container() {
         } else {
             strcat(cmd, " --gpus all");
         }
+        // All GPUs are passed into the container, but the task must only use
+        // the one the client assigned to it. Otherwise all tasks of a host with
+        // several GPUs run on the first one (CUDA's default device).
+        // CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES uses CUDA's device order, the same order the
+        // client uses for its device numbers (not the PCI order of nvidia-smi
+        // and the CDI device names).
+        //
+        if (aid.gpu_device_num >= 0 && !strncasecmp(aid.gpu_type, "nvidia", 6)) {
+            snprintf(buf, sizeof(buf), " -e CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=%d", aid.gpu_device_num);
+            strcat(cmd, buf);
+            wlog("GPU: %s device %d assigned by the client (CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=%d)\n",
+                aid.gpu_type, aid.gpu_device_num, aid.gpu_device_num
+            );
+        }
     }
 
     // web graphics
